Sure, in C you can use loops to repeat code blocks of code over and over again.  Some common types of loops are “for” loops, “while” loops, and “do-while” loops.  For example:

for (i=0; i < n; i++) {
    printf("%d ", x);
}

This loop will print the integers 0 through n to the console, one at a time.  I mentioned the “for” loop, which stands for “for loop”.  A for loop looks something like this:

for (i=0; i < n; i++) {
    if (x < 0) {
        x = -x;
    } else if (x > 0) {
        x = 5 * x;
    }
    printf("%d ", x);
}

